{
 "goal": "We need avoid further wrong guesses. Look at three demos' output patterns as representations of something standard, infer test (6,7) mask. Previous answers translationally inferred and failed; perhaps generated by motion of 3/line positions with parity. Be concise and exact.",
 "context": "Demo1 input has single 3 at (5,6), output mask rowwise: r1 c2,c4-10; r2 c2,c4,c10; r3 c2,c4,c6-8,c10; r4-r5 c2,c4,c6,c8,c10; r6 c2,c4,c8,c10; r7 c2,c4-8,c10; r8 c2,c10; r9 c2-10; r11 c1-11. Demo2 seed (6,6): r2 c4-10;r3 c4,c10;r4 c4,c6-8,c10;r5-r7 c4,c6,c8,c10;r8 c4-8,c10;r9 c4,c10;r10 c2-10. Demo3 seed (5,5):r1 c3-6;r2 c3;r3 c3,c5-7;r4-r5 c3,c5,c7;r6 c3,c7;r7 c3-7. Inputs have scattered 2s, all remain and cover any drawn 3. Test seed (6,7), 2s at (1,11),(2,2),(2,7),(4,2),(6,4),(6,9),(9,1),(10,2),(10,11),(11,7). Three guesses that translated D1 or D2 mask have been incorrect. Need infer actual process.",
 "tasks": [
  {
   "goal": "Geometric pattern inference, likely square spiral. Produce test output exact mask.",
   "context": "All data in parent, and previous translations failed.",
   "role": "leaf",
   "output_schema": {}
  },
  {
   "goal": "Independent ARC solving; do not assume translation. Look for digit/shape pattern and seed coordinate impacts.",
   "context": "Need exact candidate grid for (6,7), three wrong attempts.",
   "role": "leaf",
   "output_schema": {}
  }
 ],
 "role": "orchestrator",
 "output_schema": {},
 "background": true,
 "action": "spawn",
 "subagent_id": "",
 "message": ""
}

r,c=6,7
obstacles={(1,11),(2,2),(2,7),(4,2),(6,4),(6,9),(9,1),(10,2),(10,11),(11,7)}
# one-based spiral: N,E,S,W, lengths 2,2,4,4,...; stop before first 2 or after leaving grid
D=[(-1,0),(0,1),(1,0),(0,-1)]
mask={(r,c)}
step=2; d=0; stopped=None
while True:
  for _ in range(2):
    dr,dc=D[d%4]
    for i in range(step):
      nr,nc=r+dr,c+dc
      if (nr,nc) in obstacles:
        stopped=(nr,nc); break
      if not (1<=nr<=11 and 1<=nc<=11):
        stopped='edge'; break
      r,c=nr,nc; mask.add((r,c))
    if stopped: break
    d+=1
  if stopped: break
  step+=2
rows=[''.join('3' if (rr,cc) in mask else '.' for cc in range(1,12)) for rr in range(1,12)]
print('stop=',stopped,'count=',len(mask)); print('\n'.join(rows)); print({rr:[cc for (r0,cc) in sorted(mask) if r0==rr] for rr in range(1,12) if any(r0==rr for r0,cc in mask)})

